# Every directory pattern in this file is anchored with a leading slash, and that is not a style
# preference. An unanchored `foo/` matches a directory named `foo` at *any* depth, including a
# Java package - and because the result is an *ignored* file rather than an untracked one, it
# never shows up in `git status`. It has bitten this repo twice: `config/` kept
# eu.nordtal.s2.paymentsbot.config out of the first commits, and `run/` kept
# eu.nordtal.s2.updater.run out of the repository until the CI build failed on it.
#
# The cost of anchoring is that a build directory in a place no pattern lists is not ignored. That
# failure is loud - the files appear as untracked in `git status` - which is exactly the trade we
# want. `:checkSourcesTracked` is the net under all of this; see build-logic.

### Build output ###
/.gradle/
/*/.gradle/
/build/
/*/build/
/.kotlin/
/*/.kotlin/
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

### Secrets and runtime state. This repo is public - nothing below may ever be committed. ###
gradle.properties.local
*.env
.env
bunq-config.conf

# Runtime working directories of a server started in place.
/config/
/*/config/
/run/
/*/run/

